{{!< default}}
{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     docs-section.hbs — one documentation section.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     ⚠ ANOTHER NAME THE LIVE routes.yaml ASKS FOR. Nine content-less routes
     point at it, each binding a tag:

         /docs/getting-started/   → data: tag.getting-started
         /docs/account-profile/   → data: tag.account-profile
         … seven more

     All nine have been returning HTTP 400 with no template to render.

     ── THIS IS THE MODEL abstract/collections.md §05 ARGUES AGAINST ─────────
     Decision 0004 records why: nine hand-routed `data: tag.x` entries mean a
     routes.yaml edit AND a partial edit to add a tenth section, and in
     practice nobody ever added one. The decided model gives each section a
     backing POST (#docs-section) so a section is a piece of content, not a
     deployment.

     That decision stands. This file does NOT reopen it — it stops nine live
     URLs erroring while the old model is still the one deployed. When the
     sections become posts, these nine routes go and so does this file.

     ── data: tag.x GIVES A TAG AND ITS POSTS, NOT A POST ───────────────────
     So there is no {{#post}} here and no body to render: the section's
     description comes from the TAG's own description field in Ghost Admin.
     A section with no description draws no lede rather than an empty one.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--tight">
    <div class="ns-band__inner">
        <div class="ns-band__head">
            <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "// Documentation"}}</span>
            {{#tag}}
                <h1 class="ns-band__title">{{name}}</h1>
                {{#if description}}<p class="ns-band__lede">{{description}}</p>{{/if}}
            {{/tag}}
        </div>

        {{#if posts}}
            {{!-- .ns-tree, not a card grid: a reader in documentation is
                 finding, not browsing. The argument is in partials/docs/index.hbs. --}}
            <ul class="ns-tree">
                {{#foreach posts}}
                    <li><a class="ns-tree__node" href="{{url}}"><span class="ns-tree__label">{{title}}</span></a></li>
                {{/foreach}}
            </ul>
            {{> "pagination"}}
        {{else}}
            {{> "empty" title=(t "Nothing in this section yet")}}
        {{/if}}
    </div>
</section>
